              "text": "You can download the latest version of Python directly from the official **Python Software Foundation** website:\n\n* **Official Downloads Page:** [python.org/downloads](https://www.python.org/downloads/)\n\n### What is the latest version?\nThe latest stable version is **Python 3.14.5**. \n\n### How to Install it:\nWhen you visit the official downloads page, the website will automatically detect your operating system (Windows, macOS, Linux, etc.) and recommend the correct installer.\n\n* **Windows:** Download the installer and run it. **Important:** During setup, make sure to check the box that says **\"Add python.exe to PATH\"** before clicking \"Install Now.\" This ensures you can run Python from your command prompt.\n* **macOS:** You can download the `.pkg` installer from the website, or if you use the [Homebrew](https://brew.sh/) package manager, you can install it via your terminal by running:\n  ```bash\n  brew install python\n  ```\n* **Linux:** Python comes pre-installed on most Linux distributions. If you want to update to the latest version, it is usually best to use your system's package manager (e.g., `sudo apt update && sudo apt install python3` on Ubuntu/Debian).",
